# Extract ingest lock (do not regress)

Anthony signed off (2026-10-04): NexCourse accepts customer Word/PDF/PPT as real uploads. Do not require a NexCourse PPT template. `npm test` must stay green (`src/lib/extractQuality.test.ts`).

Anthony reversed the extract-first wait (2026-10-06): show Build now / Review immediately; extract after Continue.

## Invariants (code, not prompts)

- **Offer Storyboard vs Content file** on the upload chooser immediately (`defaultSourceModeFromFileName` + `shouldOfferStoryboardChoice` in [`src/lib/storyboardSource.ts`](src/lib/storyboardSource.ts)). Filename containing “storyboard” defaults to Storyboard; do not wait for extract. Do not wait for a perfect screen-per-slide spec. **Content file is the left card; Storyboard is the right card.**
- **Build now / Review immediately.** [`UploadPathModal`](src/components/builder/UploadPathModal.tsx) shows path cards and Continue as soon as the file is chosen. Do not hide the cards behind extract. Extract runs in `runAnalysis` after Continue.
- **Build now / Review copy.** Name both paths when mentioning Course Settings. Do not say “both options” above the cards.
- **Thin / image-only** (`assessExtract` in [`src/lib/extractQuality.ts`](src/lib/extractQuality.ts)): warn, do not block. Image-only is under ~80 words; thin is under ~250. Warn after extract (analysis), not by locking Continue.
- **Help/FAQ, not a blocker.** Help widget + homepage file-types FAQ: PPT+notes is most reliable; Word/PDF follow extractable text. Do not refuse Word/PDF.
- **Content file extract reaches outline and hydrate.** [`fileSourceConfigFromExtract`](src/lib/storyboardSource.ts) passes the **full** extract + `isSourceConversion` for raw uploads. Analyze/outline pack later pages via [`contentFileCoverageWindow`](src/lib/storyboardSource.ts) (`CONTENT_FILE_COVERAGE_CHARS` = 36k). Hydrate uses [`contentFileHydrateExcerpt`](src/lib/storyboardSource.ts) per module — do not dump the whole PPT into every chunk, and do not slice only the first 12k. Storyboard still uses `storyboardSourceWindow`. A storyboard screen that says “Question 1 of 3” still becomes **N Knowledge Check slides**, same as a content file — never one 3-of-3 seq. `npm test` must stay green (`src/lib/extractQuality.test.ts`).
- **Word tables stay text.** `tableToMarkdown` in [`server.js`](server.js) flattens tables. Do not replace them with `[Table — see original document]`.
- **Skip embedded Word images** so extract status is not a huge HTML blob (`mammoth` `convertImage` skip).
- **Sleeping API is warmup, not a bad file.** `runAnalysis` waits on `/api/health` (`ANALYSIS_WARM_TIMEOUT_MS`) before parse/AI. Timeouts, 524s, and `Failed to fetch` use `isAnalysisTransient` → cold-start countdown, not Analysis Failed. Do not restore a generic “reading your file” overlay for Render spin-down.
- **Generate / outline / Add content wait the same way.** `hydrateCourse`, `generateOutline`, and `handleGenerateAddedContent` **await** `waitForApiWarm`. `executeAnthropicAI` retries 503/`COLD_START`/`Failed to fetch` after warmup (not 401/402/trial) and retries an empty/`{}` payload once. Hydrate **throws** auth/transient failures immediately. Empty/unparseable JSON still runs Tier 2 and per-slide, then throws instead of writing “This slide covers key content…” stubs (`shouldAbortHydrateLadder`). `/api/ai` must not `recordAiSuccess` on empty text (`EMPTY_AI`). Outline parse uses `OUTLINE_PARSE_MESSAGE`, never `Critical Data Failure`. Edit → Regenerate keeps the existing slide and the Edit drawer (`REGEN_KEEP_SLIDE_MESSAGE`). Do not fire-and-forget warmup on Generate. `npm test` must stay green (`src/lib/analysisErrors.test.ts`).
- **Empty AI JSON is not “paste more source”.** Add content uses [`formatAddContentFailure`](src/lib/analysisErrors.ts) / `ADD_CONTENT_EMPTY_MESSAGE` (“Generate in Add content”). Review hydrate uses [`formatHydrateFailure`](src/lib/analysisErrors.ts) / `HYDRATE_EMPTY_MESSAGE` (“Generate Course again”). Outline uses [`formatOutlineFailure`](src/lib/analysisErrors.ts) / `OUTLINE_PARSE_MESSAGE`. Do not tell the author to paste more when `/api/ai` returned `{}` or unparseable text. Do not tell Add content to click Generate Course.
- **Review hydrate failure stays on Review.** [`hydrateCourse`](src/App.tsx) clears `error` before a retry. [`CourseReviewPage`](src/components/builder/CourseReviewPage.tsx) must not swap the page for `renderProgressState` / Generation Failed — that hid Generate Course and Start Over wiped extract while leaving the file (“File Ready”). Empty JSON copy tells the author to click Generate Course again, not Start Over. Account Course Settings must not swap to that overlay either. `npm test` must stay green (`src/lib/analysisErrors.test.ts`).
- **Outline failure retries on the tab you are on.** A missing outline disables Generate Course. The Review header becomes **Try again** / **Generate Structure** and calls [`onRegenerateOutline`](src/App.tsx). Do not leave retry only on Course structure. Leave Review / go home / open account Course Settings / land on `/upload` clears `error`. Direct `/upload` also clears `uploadedFile` so File Ready cannot sit on a wiped extract.
- **Oversized upload Try Again is not a no-op.** A file over 50MB does not keep `uploadedFile`. The overlay **Choose another file** returns to `/upload`. Do not `return` from Try Again when the file was never stored.
- **Dropped draft fetch is not “corrupted”.** [`formatDraftOpenFailure`](src/lib/analysisErrors.ts) maps HTML/JSON/524/Failed to fetch to retry copy. Do not restore “It may be corrupted.”

## How to change this

Change the helpers and add a failing test first. Do not restore an extract-first Continue lock to “speed up” upload.
